#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:2 fe0f06153b4c42979619322c23049af0
msgid "The library page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:4 f5be5d953d5047669dc974e4e3888013
msgid ""
"One library, and everything that can be done to it. If you are working on"
" a library, this is the page to be on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:7 1fb8dae26431457c8ea6ad5e7b498597
msgid ""
"Open it from **Libraries** in the header and click a library, or go "
"straight to ``/libraries/detail/<id>/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:10 50e9664e825a4028b86e5269b70c74d8
msgid "The library page for library 50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:19 0dfb93eecd7b411ba14755da533fda5b
msgid "What is on it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:21 c8c5edac4198403fbff6fecd55bb605c
msgid "**Library Overview**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:22 978109663b6c4f32bdb1aa001153a1d3
msgid ""
"What the library is - its id, vendor and model - and the buttons that act"
" on the whole of it: Tapes, Monitor, Sync, Refresh, Stop and Remove."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:25 66770d82efb74fffbe432ecea409f975
msgid "**Capacity & Statistics**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:26 1e81c980cfd34a5fab3f2e228b019a4c
msgid ""
"Slots, how many hold a tape, how many are free, how many drives, and when"
" the console last read the configuration. The **Empty slots** box changes"
" how many spare slots the library has; see :doc:`../tapes/create`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:30 430a0c27dae54254a721388b24fed8a3
msgid "**Manage this library**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:31 32939ce6ba2d44408ba27326527d1708
msgid ""
"Fifteen links, in four groups - Tapes, Drives, The robot, The library. "
"Each one carries the library with it, so the page it opens is already set"
" to this one. This is the hub: you should rarely need to pick the library"
" again once you are here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:36 2dffceb3e45540d188c848eed02dbcb5
msgid "Manage this library: fifteen links in four groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:40 0360c59666aa44e79b4aac66b1bd841f
msgid "**Tape Drives**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:41 ab5b66b6502449ac8c1571878c311450
msgid ""
"What each drive is doing, refreshed every five seconds, then a card per "
"drive with its SCSI address and serial. See :doc:`../using/watching`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:44 8e4e10a707d24ecdb3315644be7065af
msgid "The drive panel: what each drive is doing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:48 fd0979dbd4ad4e3986d8b2d4c2ee6b2c
msgid "**Tapes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:49 898db3d3f9db4f3398990c041abe2708
msgid "A tile per tape, with a bar for how full it is and how much room is left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:51 ae71a8a45a37496784f04f7d9e033e19
msgid "Two tape tiles, each with a bar for how full the cartridge is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:55 459d8197f0964ff2adfb5d3d6e353492
msgid "**Technical Specifications**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:56 aa67ddf3a4cc49c1bcea406c25601fb1
msgid ""
"The SCSI address, the serial, the NAA, and where MHVTL keeps this "
"library's files. Useful when something else on the host disagrees with "
"the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:61 5c3509fd00794dc8b4538d34cce6b445
msgid "The same thing from the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:63 d24068cfd90c43f6b77f770528199e65
msgid ""
"There is no single command that prints the whole page, because the page "
"answers four questions. These are them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:73 e7a669df913644f4926f26a75ac3799f
msgid ""
"``library show`` reads ``device.conf``; ``status library`` asks the robot"
" through ``mtx``; ``status activity`` asks the drive daemons directly. "
"When the first two disagree, the library was changed without being "
"restarted - the console says so on the page, and ``mhvtl`` says so on the"
" command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:79 448651b42e324ce8b34373f63b369440
msgid "The buttons, and what they run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:82 d0fd36a30d9b4be4afb7f5255b17d968
msgid "Button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:82 55a5aedd0c9d47bf91c7c03877e5db2c
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:84 b9ff551ba9ce489499bf2722fe73c9ce
msgid "**Sync**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:84 f2ca90f8157349628847ace051fccaf0
msgid ""
"Reads the MHVTL configuration again and updates the console's record of "
"it. Changes nothing on the host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:86 beec7c4da3914f09a7614f16373f540c
msgid "**Refresh**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:86 86c850c2722845b8b57a0b17654d74ee
msgid "Reloads the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:87 f3936788db0743219b3ed1d08a0441dc
msgid "**Stop**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:87 92779b59c5d3479d8194c958beacce9f
msgid ""
"Stops this library's daemons - the robot and its drives. The same as "
"``sudo mhvtl service stop --library 50``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:89 ed34bdc6476849cf853f4ac1f46d8905
msgid "**Monitor**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:89 a29a640cecd14e74926d9abdf5087ac8
msgid ""
"Opens the monitor page: service state, drives online, slots, errors, and "
"what the drives are doing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:91 eb058facd3a4414a99b1cd4d8abfb83b
msgid "**Remove**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:91 3b28598a4eee4b6db9a1275cfc3eb5de
msgid ""
"Deletes the library from ``device.conf``. Its tapes are not deleted "
"unless you ask for that. The same as ``sudo mhvtl library delete 50``; "
"read :doc:`remove` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:97 53c162627305436490cfbc524687def3
msgid "If the page says 404"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:99 762bc512f76e45249b65c10884fb14ba
msgid ""
"A library created from the command line exists in ``device.conf`` before "
"the console's database has heard of it. Opening the page syncs it first, "
"so this should not happen; if it does, press **Sync** on the library "
"list, or check that the library is really there:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:108 deb286d3fe7b4113bcd408071250506d
msgid ""
"If it is in that list and the page still refuses, the console cannot read"
" ``/etc/mhvtl``. It runs as the user ``mhvtl-gui`` in the group "
"``mhvtl``; check that it can read the directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/the-library-page.rst:116 f00bed7d9e1b4daeb8f5f6ec8fcab7a2
msgid ""
"If that fails - reinstalling MHVTL can reset the directory's owner - give"
" it back the group the package set when it was installed:"
msgstr ""

